    "notes": "drive record read from doc/tasks/0612-evidence/phase0_size_law.txt:52; The 28 rows of the retained capture table (columns `pixelSize`, `scale`, `asp`, `uni`) are the same 28 rows the fixture already carries as per-case columns, so this block is a re-projection and was cross-read against both. EXCLUDED as the stand: `image` / `clip_px` (512x256 and 256x512), which is the loaded image asset the backdrop points at, in the same class as a load-mesh step. EXCLUDED as instrument calibration, and mentioned here rather than dropped silently: the front-orthographic view at 32 px per world metre (`instrument.px_per_metre` = 32.0, `pixel_size_meaning` = 1/32) -- it is the ruler, not a parameter of the operation, and every measured_px column is denominated in it. Case A2pre carries the same values as case A and differs only in ORDER (the size channel was written BEFORE the clip was linked instead of after), which the values map cannot express."
  },
  "why_this_fixture_exists": "Until 2026-08-20 this law had no toolcard, no fixture and no test -- it existed as one evidence .txt and a paragraph in an agent's memory. It is the size law for an entire item type we ship, and it overturned three separate candidates in the design plan that produced it, so re-deriving it from scratch would be expensive.",
  "instrument": {
    "view": "front orthographic, ortho scale 32",
    "px_per_metre": 32.0,
    "calibration": "a 1 m reference quad moved a known 10 m in X -> 320.00 px; null control (move back to 0) -> zero changed pixels",
    "pixel_size_meaning": "ILxView3D::PixelSize() read 0.03125 = 1/32, i.e. metres per pixel in an ortho view, exactly 1 / the SetScale argument",
    "gate": "the reference's own documented worked example, 512 px at 10 mm -> 5.12 m, reproduced to +0.16 px before any case was scored"
  },
  "law": {
    "inputs": "W,H = clip pixel size; p = pixelSize channel (metres per image pixel, default 0.01); sx,sy = item scale X/Y",
    "sz_has_no_effect": true,
    "base_extent": {
      "uniform=0, aspect=1 (DEFAULT)": "(W*p, H*p)",
      "uniform=0, aspect=0": "(H*p, H*p)  -- the image HEIGHT on BOTH axes",
      "uniform=1, aspect=1": "(W/H, 1.0) metres",
      "uniform=1, aspect=0": "(1.0, 1.0) metres"
    },
    "scale_composition": {
      "aspect=1 (DEFAULT)": "extent = base * min(sx, sy)   -- ONE scalar, not per-axis",
      "aspect=0": "extent = (base_u * sx, base_v * sy)"
    },
    "placement": "the quad is centred on the item and carried RIGIDLY by its position and rotation; scale is consumed by the extent formula and is NOT additionally applied to the quad",
    "live_not_frozen": "pixelSize is read LIVE. Rewriting it after the clip is linked resizes the plane every time (2.56 -> 5.12 -> 1.28 -> 2.56 m), and writing it before the link gives a bit-identical frame to writing it after (case A2pre)."
  },
  "tolerance": {
    "residual_px": 0.96,
    "why": "rasterisation quantisation, not model error: the two worst rows predict 40.96 px and rasterise to 40. Stated in pixels because that is the unit the error lives in."
  },
